g","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day","interior"]}]},"attendance":16180},"article":{"headline":"Air Force runs for 429 yards in 52-3 rout of UTEP","description":"— Evan Medders threw two touchdown passes, Air Force ran for 429 yards, and the Falcons swamped UTEP 52-3 on Friday night.","story":"AIR FORCE ACADEMY, Colo. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5306440/evan-medders\" target=\"_new\">Evan Medders</a> threw two touchdown passes, Air Force ran for 429 yards, and the Falcons swamped UTEP 52-3 on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              Three of the Falcons' four completed passes went for touchdowns, two by Medders and one by <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5223110/maguire-martin\" target=\"_new\">Maguire Martin</a>. Medders' touchdowns were 77 yards to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5238876/jonah-dawson\" target=\"_new\">Jonah Dawson</a> and 31 yards to <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5223149/adam-hrynciw\" target=\"_new\">Adam Hrynciw</a>. Martin's only pass attempt was a connection with <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5388367/major-quin\" target=\"_new\">Major Quin</a> on a 35-yard score.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5223131/rocco-conti\" target=\"_new\">Rocco Conti</a> led Air Force with 64 yards rushing and 18 players had rushing attempts for the Falcons (9-2, 5-2 Mountain West).\n\n\r\n              Air Force had 586 total yards to UTEP's 116. First downs were 27-6 in favor of Air Force.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5078912/jayden-wilson\" target=\"_new\">Jayden Wilson</a> had 12 total tackles for the Miners (1-10, 0-7).\n\n\r\n              Air Force and UTEP played for the first time since 1995 when both schools were members of the Western Athletic Conference. Air Force leads the overall series, 15-1, including an 8-0 mark at home.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Air Force wraps up the regular season at New Mexico next Friday.\n\n\r\n              UTEP finishes at Northern Illinois on Nov. 28. ------\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"https://apnews.com/newsletters\">Sign up for Top 25 poll alerts here</a>. Visit <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/ap-top-25-college-football-poll\">the Top 25 here</a> and see AP’s full <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/college-football\">college football coverage here.</a>","published":"2026-11-21T05:03:31Z"}}